  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Red lines: what the architecture tests reject",
      "items": [
        "A Module that references another Module's implementation, even unused: ModuleBoundaryTests, \u201cNo module references another modules implementation\u201d.",
        "Contracts that reference the Kit or a Module: ModuleBoundaryTests, \u201cContracts reference nothing from the kit and no module\u201d.",
        "Feature code that saves, commits, writes in bulk, opens a transaction or calls a Kit step such as the Unit of Work, the Outbox or BeginOperation (ADR 0003): FeatureCodeTests, \u201cNo module saves commits or touches its database and only the unit of work does\u201d.",
        "A Module or its Contracts that name a Wolverine or JasperFx type: FeatureCodeTests, \u201cNo module contract or messaging contract names a transport type\u201d.",
        "A Module, its Contracts or a Host that implements a pipeline contract: PipelineContractTests, \u201cNo module or host implements a pipeline contract and the kit implements each\u201d."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What holds the boundary",
      "items": [
        "A Module's only public types are its Composition Root and what its Host implements for it: ModuleBoundaryTests, \u201cA modules only public types are its composition root and what its host implements for it\u201d.",
        "The Gateway runs only its own Module's commands and queries, each as one Operation in a new scope begun with the Module; another Module's command throws.",
        "The Unit of Work a Module's Composition Root registers is keyed by the Module, and the Operation's Module picks it; a Module that handles a command without one fails while the Host is composed.",
        "Each Kit package references exactly what PackageGraph allows: PackageGraphTests, \u201cA kit packages references and closure are those section c allows\u201d."
      ]
    }
  ]
